      "observed": "REG3 output and sense pins are on +3.3V, but the MCU supply pins are not connected to that rail: the FCC2 VDD pins and NAVC2 VDD pins are listed as unconnected. NAVC2 VBAT is on +3V3, a separate net from +3.3V, and NAVC2 VSS pins are on a separate net from GND.",
      "expected": "The specification says the 3.3 V rail feeds both MCUs and sensors. Both MCUs' VDD pins should be connected to the regulated 3.3 V rail, and their ground pins should be connected to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG3\") (pin \"1\") ... (node (ref \"REG3\") (pin \"2\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)\") ... (net (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad27)\") ... (net (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad50)\") ... (net (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad75)\") ... (net (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad100)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)\") ... (net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad32)\") ... (net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad48)\") ... (net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad64)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(NAVC2-VSS-Pad18)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"18\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"63\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "As represented, neither MCU has its VDD pins powered from the regulator; the NAVC also lacks a connection from its listed VSS pins to GND. The MCUs therefore cannot operate as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["HSE1", "HSE3", "FCC2", "NAVC2"],
      "pins": ["FCC2.5", "FCC2.12", "FCC2.13", "FCC2.37", "NAVC2.5", "NAVC2.6"],
      "nets": ["NET0089", "NET0029", "NET0031", "Net-(C1-Pad1)", "Net-(C54-Pad1)", "Net-(FCC2-PH0)", "VREF+_FCC", "Net-(NAVC2-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC2-PH1)"],
      "observed": "The FCC crystal HSE3 connects to FCC2.5 (PE6) and, through R32, FCC2.37 (PE7), rather than the MCU's PH0/PH1 pins. FCC2.12 (PH0) is connected only to C23, while FCC2.13 (PH1) is on VREF+_FCC. The NAVC crystal HSE1 nets likewise do not connect to NAVC2.5 (PH0) or NAVC2.6 (PH1).",
      "expected": "The specification calls for a 25 MHz HSE crystal on both MCUs; each crystal should connect to its MCU's HSE oscillator pins, with the associated load network.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0089\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")) (node (ref \"HSE3\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0029\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\")) (node (ref \"R32\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(FCC2-PH0)\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"12\") (pinfunction \"PH0\")) (node (ref \"C23\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"VREF+_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"PH1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0031\") ... (node (ref \"HSE1\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(C1-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"HSE1\") (pin \"3\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The external crystals are not connected to the MCUs' HSE oscillator pins, so the specified external clock source will not function. The oscillator pins are instead left improperly connected or assigned to other nets.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: the MCU supply and ground connections are missing or split from the regulated rails, and the external crystal networks are not connected to the MCUs' HSE pins. These connectivity faults prevent the board from behaving as specified."
}

